Z||000000||Ayrow||11-15-2001||04:04 AM||||Hi everybody!<P>I found this site and fell in love with it so I regestered and plan on becoming a big part of it.<P>I have owned 4 Fieros ('84 SE, 86 GT, '88 Formula, and my '87 GT) and currently have an '87 GT (blue) in storage that will not be touched anytime soon.<P>Here's what I need help with:<P>I want to start from scratch and build and awesome car from an '88 GT.<P>First I have to find one.....<P>I have been doing a lot of reading on the net over the last few days and have come to the conclusion that if I am going to buy another Fiero to restore and modify, I'd better know what I want to do and where I want to wind up.<P>I have been out of it for 10 years and have learned that people are doing all kinds of interesting things.<P>What are the most popular and cost-effective things to do. A new Engine???  A Cadillac Engine??? (couldn't belive this the first time I hear it).<P>Are people actually able to paint the Fiero effectivly now?  This was a big problem in the past..<P>I want to create a great '88 GT that handles and performs with the best of them.  Doesn't have to be a show car, just fun to drive.<P>Sorry for the long post, but I am not sure where to start.<P>Any opinions or leads in finding a used '88 GT would be great.<P>Thanks you,<P>Ayrow<BR>||||reg||10
